  "gaps": [
    "https://developer.clip.mx/reference/pruebas is a client-rendered SPA and returned no content to a plain fetch. The content was read from the official https://developer.clip.mx/llms-full.txt, which mirrors the portal pages. The canonical page URLs inside it point to developer.payclip.com, which refused connections from this environment.",
    "Codes are status_detail.code values returned with status 'rejected' on Checkout Transparente POST /payments. Messages are quoted from the table. RE-ISS02 is 'Do not honour' in the table but 'Do not honor' in the 3DS section.",
    "The test card table gives only a text reason (e.g. 'Not sufficient funds'). It does not state which status_detail.code each card returns. Mapping 'Not sufficient funds' to RE-ISS01, 'Do not honor' to RE-ISS02, 'Restricted card' to RE-ISS03 and 'Exceeds withdrawal amount limit' to RE-ISS08 matches the message text but is an inference, not documented.",
    "The error page also documents an error object with error.decline_code (only for processing_error), but lists no decline_code literals for Checkout Transparente. UPPER_CASE codes such as INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS and DO_NOT_HONOR appear only in the SDK Terminal (card-present) table, so they are left out.",
    "No 3DS test cards are documented for sandbox.",
    "CVV rule correction vs repo presets: the docs say any 3- or 4-digit number, not just 'any CVV'.",
    "byCard lists Mexico cards only. The docs also list Visa, Mastercard and Amex USA cards with the same 5-scenario pattern, and say international cards need KYC.",
    "The docs give no per-code retry guidance for status_detail. They only give HTTP-level guidance: retry 429/500/502/503, never other 4xx. retryable=true only for issuer-offline and inoperative codes (processing errors). retryable=false only for pick-up, expired and invalid number."
  ]
}
